sentences.t:
Ac veluti montis saxum de vertice praeceps
cum ruit avulsum vento, seu turbidus imber
proluit aut annis solvit sublapsa vetustas;

sentences.l:
And as from a mountain's a rock top headlong
when it rushes, torn away by the wind, or a turbid rainstorm
has washed it out, or with years loosened it, creeping beneath, old age;

sentences.t:
Ac velut ingenti Sila summove Taburno
cum duo conversis inimica in proelia tauri
frontibus incurrunt;

sentences.l:
And as on huge Sila or on the top of Taburnus
when two, with turned, into hostile battle, bulls
brows charge;

sentences.t:
pavidi cessere magistri,
stat pecus omne metu mutum mussantque iuvencae,
quis nemori imperitet, quem tota armenta sequantur;

sentences.l:
frightened have withdrawn the herdsmen,
stands the herd all with fear mute, and wonder the heifers
who the grove will rule, whom all the herds will follow;

sentences.t:
illi inter sese multa vi volnera miscent
cornuaque obnixi infigunt et sanguine largo
colla armosque lavant;

sentences.l:
they among themselves with much force wounds exchange,
and horns, straining, drive in, and with blood abundant
necks and shoulders bathe;

sentences.t:
Iuppiter ipse duas aequato examine lances
sustinet et fata imponit diversa duorum,
quem damnet labor et quo vergat pondere letum;

postquam arma dei ad Volcania ventumst,
mortalis mucro glacies ceu futilis ictu
dissiluit;

sentences.l:
after it came to the arms of the god, Vulcanian,
the mortal blade, like ice brittle, at the stroke
flew apart;

So, out of his mind, different in flight he seeks parts of the plain, Turnus,
and now hither, now thither, uncertain he weaves circles;
for on all sides with a dense the Teucrians have shut him in, ring,
and here a vast marsh, here steep walls hem him in.
